ight breast biopsy with needle localization   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm oriented breast tissue with a detached localization wire  with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The long axis is superior to inferior  and the specimen is inked as follow  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  and lateral yellow  The parenchyma is grossly fatty with focal hemorrhage  No masses or calcifications are grossly identified  The specimen is entirely and sequentially submitted from superior to inferior as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma with anterior  posterior  medial and lateral margins including the hemorrhagic areas  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  The foci of invasive carcinoma are very small  Both invasive and in situ carcinoma show similar staining  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  486  to chromosome 17 signals  100  in 30 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from 18    2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  report_end  , Present.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 07 CLINICAL DATA  Status post needle localization                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   RIGHT BREAST MASS    BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   1    REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED   SEE NOTE   2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA   99    EXTENSIVE  MIXED COMEDO  MICROPAPILLARY  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES WITH FOCAL NEUROENDOCRINE FEATURES  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  SEE NOTE   3  RADIAL SCAR  MICROSCOPIC  NOTE  A single microscopic focus of infiltrating ductal carcinoma is seen in slide H  Due to the microscopic size of the invasive carcinoma  accurate grading of the tumor is not possible  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Intraductal carcinoma is present in seven of nine slides and spares at least 2 0cm  Microcalcifications are associated with the intraductal carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 40                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE IN SITU TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE IN SITU TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain invasive tumor cells  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm fragment of breast tissue with localizing wire in place  Inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Submitted entirely in cassettes A through I  Gross Description by  KEITH KWAN  MD Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   NO GROSS EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Chin lee Wu  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY , Present.
