Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 12 12 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  WITH A MAXIMUM SPAN OF REMOVED_DATE CM  MEASURED FROM SLIDES B AND C   EXTENDING TO AN INKED CAUTERIZED MARGIN ACROSS A BROAD FRONT  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   HEALING ASPIRATION SITE  NOTE  By immunoperoxidase methods  the infiltrating tumor cells stain strongly for cytokeratin  but show unconvincing to faint non membrane staining for e cadherin  consistent with the morphological impression of lobular carcinoma  A small population of e cadherin negative cells within ducts have a similar cytological appearance  The invasive tumor cells are widely scattered in fibrous parenchyma and mostly dispersed as single cells  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 17 18                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block B   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  01 AUG 03 at 14 28     FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION Addendum     RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block B   HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 03 at 17 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm piece of yellow tan fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is firm and somewhat rubbery on palpation  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal firm  tan white tissue admixed with softer yellow adipose tissue  The specimen is taken entirely in cassettes A C  Resident  MINDY J  HULL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Absent.
