orly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm hemorrhagic area which abuts the inferior anterior margin and comes to 0 1cm of the medial margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Hemorrhagic area to closest margin  B E  Mass to closest margins  F  Lateral margin  radial sections   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast biopsy posterior lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue with localization wire in place  No orientation is provided  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hemorrhagic area which communicates with the margin  possibly consistent with previous biopsy site  Surrounding the defect is focally nodular dense grey white fibrous tissue  There are no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as G N  with the area designated by the localization wire in G J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axilla sentinel node  are two round tan pink rubbery lymph nodes which range from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm in greatest dimension  The smallest is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette O  The largest is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette P Q  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast final shaved margin  superior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of unoriented fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette R Y  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast final shaved margin  inferior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm aggregate of unoriented cauterized fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette Z GG  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  JULIA TURBINER  M D    