ed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  excision of cancer site  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 8cm irregular portion of tan yellow to focally hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue  which has a single stitch designating the medial border  and 2 stitches designating the superior border of the specimen  The specimen is partially surfaced at the anterior aspect by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm wrinkled white skin ellipse  which has been previously dyed blue and has 2 needle localization wires extending from it  The specimen is received with a specimen radiograph  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  medial   green  and lateral   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned along the superior to the inferior axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm cavity containing red brown  hemorrhagic material  which appears to represent prior biopsy site  The cavity is surrounded by dense gray white fibrous tissue with focal areas of tan yellow fat necrosis  The cavity extends to within 0 8cm from the lateral  1 1cm from the posterior  2 0cm from the anterior  2 5cm from the medial  2 0cm from the superior  and  3cm from the inferior margins  The remainder of the breast parenchyma cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with a moderate amount of interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue  No other discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior end  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior end  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the biopsy cavity to the nearest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the fibrous breast parenchyma away from the biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sequential secti